# Water Test - BONANZA's WATER test course (SPEC.md 130.36), built only by the BZWATER=1 knob, as
# shapes.bbc is by BZSHAPES=1.  It is NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES and makes it the
# pathway's pad 0, so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.
#
# The owner's sketch (docs/plans/bounce-bonanza/water-sketch.png): a WALKWAY of floor cells 3 units up, one
# of them WATER, flush with it, its ripples drawn; under it a glass-walled column 3 units deep; at the bottom
# of the column's FRONT face an ARCH, out onto a lower path running toward the viewer.  Rubber and glass roll
# across the water at the walkway's level; steel sinks down the column and rolls out of the front.
#  - a DECK 6 units up at the left, a ramp up to it from the walkway: in it a DEEP column (4, 8), 6 units to its
#    bed - steel sinks the whole way and leaves by a front arch; its ripples animate ALWAYS (a lone column);
#  - the start on the deck, a RUBBER pad on the walkway, a STEEL pad beside the first column (its window holds
#    the water: the swap refills it);
#  - the sketch's column at (8, 8), on the walkway's front row, its arch +y onto the lower yard; its ripples
#    animate while a ball is in it;
#  - a ROW of four columns (11 - 14, 8), one arch at the far end ((14, 8) +y); in front of the other three a
#    ledge a unit up, which seals them at the bed (and shows their glass); steel walks the bed under the row;
#    (12, 8) ripples while a ball is in it;
#  - a TOWER 7 units up behind the row, its front edge one cell from the water, a GLASS pad on it: glass
#    rolled off it falls 4 units - a shatter on stone, landed whole on the water;
#  - the finish (exit 0) on the yard below the first arch; exit 1, the walkway's far end, goes on to FIRST.
course WATER "Water Test"
width  128
ball   rubber
uses   water

floor rect  6  3 18  9 flat 3        # the walkway, 3 units up
floor rect  6  3  8  5 ramp x 6 8 6 3   # its ramp up to the deck
floor rect  3  3  6  9 flat 6        # the deck, 6 units up
floor rect  3  9 18 15 flat 0        # the lower yard in front of them
floor rect 11  9 14 10 flat 1        # the ledge sealing the row's three closed columns at their bed
floor rect 11  3 15  7 flat 7        # the glass drop's tower, its front edge one cell behind the row
water tile  4  8      top 6 bed 0 always 4 8    # the DEEP column, 6 units, ripples always
water tile  8  8      top 3 bed 0 ripple 8 8    # the sketch's column, ripples while a ball is in it
water rect 11  8 15 9 top 3 bed 0 ripple 12 8   # the row of four
arch  4  8 +y
arch  8  8 +y
arch 14  8 +y

pad steel   7  7
pad rubber  6  6
pad glass  13  5
start 5 6
goal tile  8 14 flat 0
goal tile 17  6 flat 3 exit 1
clock  5 13
clock 16  4
target 60
way 5 6
way 7 4
way 9 4
way 9 6
way 8 7
way 8 14
